/**
 * JISR BULK OPS - ALL-IN-ONE  v4.44.0
 * ======================================
 * One install instead of eleven. This file is the old per-module toolkit
 * (modules 01-05, 07-12, each at its latest version) placed back to back,
 * plus section 14 (Employee Groups, Business Units, Export Everything) ported
 * from the single-panel v2.1 script with its bugs fixed.
 *
 * Each module is kept byte-for-byte inside its own function scope, exactly as
 * it was when installed as a separate script, so nothing about how any tool
 * behaves has changed. They already shared one floating button, one name
 * gate, one employee-directory cache and one optional backend; now they also
 * share one install and one update.
 *
 * NOT included: 06 (standalone Tabulator tool, kept separate by design) and
 * 13 (Cloud Folder).
 *
 * INSTALLING: disable or remove the separate 01-12 scripts and the old v2.x
 * "Jisr Bulk Ops" panel script first, otherwise every tool appears twice.
 * Your name and shared-backend settings carry over automatically (they live
 * in the Jisr site's own storage, not the script's).
 *
 * Module versions bundled:
 *   01 Employee ID  v2.6.2
 *   02 Roles & Permissions  v1.5.2
 *   03 Salary Increment  v1.9.2
 *   04 Suspend Payrun Salary  v2.5.2
 *   05 GOSI Applicable Amount  v1.6.2
 *   07 Locations Manager  v1.2.2
 *   08 Job Titles  v1.3.2
 *   09 Payroll Reconciliation  v1.9.0
 *   11 Employee Contracts  v1.2.0
 *   12 Departments  v1.0.3
 *   14 Employee Groups & Business Units + Export Everything  v3.0.0
 *   15 Attendance Log Converter  v3.1.0
 *   16 GOSI Compliance — Export & Salary Check  v4.44.0
 *    0 Language follows the Jisr page (EN/AR)  v4.44.0
 */


// ###########################################################################
// ##### SECTION 0 — Language follows the Jisr page (EN/AR)  v4.48.0
// ###########################################################################

/*
 * ===========================================================================
 * SECTION 0 — Language follows the Jisr page (English / Arabic)
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Jisr marks the page language on <html lang="ar" dir="rtl"> (and keeps
 * localStorage "Locale" = "ar"/"en"). When the page is Arabic, every Jisr
 * Bulk Ops window (hub menu, tool modals, toasts, confirm/alert prompts, the
 * Payroll Reconciliation widget) is translated in place and switched to
 * right-to-left; when it's English, the original text is put back.
 *
 * How: a dictionary of the tools' own UI strings (built into this file from
 * i18n/ar-*.json at build time) is applied to text nodes and placeholder /
 * title attributes INSIDE the tools' own windows only - never to Jisr's page,
 * never to input values, and never to downloaded Excel files (templates keep
 * their English headers so re-uploads still map). Exact matches first, then
 * known "prefix + number + suffix" messages. Anything not in the dictionary
 * (mostly Jisr's own error text and employee data) stays as-is.
 *
 * Tools written after this (Attendance Log Converter) use the small API on
 * unsafeWindow.__jisrBulkOpsI18n directly: isAr(), t(en, ar), onChange(fn).
 * ===========================================================================
 */
